## KEY ARCHITECTURAL DECISIONS AND WHY
==============================================================================

### Why no framework?
The spec explicitly requires "plain PHP 8.0+, SQLite, no framework, raw cURL
for all external HTTP." Keeps the app deployable on any shared host with PHP.

### Why SQLite?
Low concurrency SaaS (one user → one conversion at a time per account).
WAL mode allows concurrent reads. No MySQL setup overhead.

### Why one-time payments only (NOT subscriptions)?
Explicitly stated in the spec. Stripe mode is "payment" (never "subscription").
PayPal intent is "CAPTURE". Subscriptions would require recurring billing logic
that is explicitly out of scope.

### Why raw <link> tag for Google Fonts (Rule 2)?
WordPress's wp_enqueue_style() runs the URL through esc_url() which encodes
the pipe character `|` in CSS API URLs like:
  https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter|Roboto
Breaking the font request. Solution: hook raw <link> tags via
add_action('wp_head', ..., 5) before any other head output.

### Why Customizer transport: 'postMessage' for live preview?
Allows JS to update CSS custom properties on the fly without page reload,
giving instant Customizer preview. The customizer_live_preview() function
enqueues inline JS that regenerates :root CSS vars from postMessage events.

### Why pre-compute variables before heredoc in prompts/functions-gen.php?
PHP does not allow the ?? operator inside {$var} heredoc interpolations:
  "{$data['colors']['primary'] ?? '#2563eb'}"  ← PARSE ERROR
Must extract to variables first:
  $default_primary = $data['colors']['primary'] ?? '#2563eb';
  Then use {$default_primary} in heredoc.

### Why fastcgi_finish_request() in convert.php?
Sends the HTTP response to the browser (showing the progress polling UI)
before the conversion actually starts. The conversion then runs server-side
after the response is flushed. JS polls /api/convert-status/{uuid} every 3s.

### Why realpath() security check in download.php?
Prevents directory traversal attacks. The download UUID comes from the URL.
Before serving any file, we resolve its real path and verify it starts with
the storage/conversions/ directory prefix.

### Why the 'parsed' status uses paid_at IS NULL check?
The conversions table status flow is:
  pending → parsed → paid → converting → complete → failed/expired
The 'parsed' status means analysis is done but payment hasn't been received.
The 'paid' status means payment webhook OR success-URL capture confirmed.

### Why ai_calls_used counter?
The conversion runs 8 AI calls (functions_php, header_footer, 1 per section,
css, js, woocommerce if needed, demo_content). Tracking ai_calls_used allows
the JS progress bar to show real progress (not just fake animation).

