## CONVERSION PIPELINE DETAILS
==============================================================================

The converter runs in this sequence (Converter.php orchestrates):

1. Parser.php: ZipArchive::extractTo() to temp dir → find source files
   - Extracts: globals.css, Layout.jsx, pages.config.js, pages/*, components/*
   - Returns array of file paths + content

2. Analyzer.php: Inspects source files
   - WooCommerce detection: 5 signal types (component names, price fields,
     entity definitions, Cart/Checkout imports, product API patterns)
   - Archetype: landing / multi-page / ecommerce
   - Color extraction: :root CSS vars + Tailwind arbitrary [#hex] classes
   - Font detection: Google Fonts @import URLs in globals.css
   - Page extraction: pages.config.js entity analysis
   - Returns structured $data array

3. Converter.php: 8 sequential Claude API calls
   a. functions_php → functions.php
   b. layout → header.php + footer.php
   c. home_section × N → template-parts/{section}.php (one call per section)
   d. page_templates → page-{slug}.php for each non-home page
   e. css → assets/css/theme.css
   f. js → assets/js/theme.js
   g. woocommerce (if $has_woocommerce) → assets/css/woocommerce.css +
      woocommerce/ template overrides
   h. demo_content → inc/demo-content.php
   Parses "=== filename.ext ===" delimiters from responses.
   Updates ai_calls_used after each call.

4. Assembler.php: Creates output directory tree
   - {output_dir}/{uuid}/{prefix}-theme/
   - Writes all generated files
   - Copies wp-skeleton/ .tpl files, replacing {PREFIX}/{THEME_NAME} etc.
   - Creates placeholder screenshot.png (GD or SVG fallback)
   - ZipArchive creates {prefix}-theme.zip
   - Returns zip path

