## CONVERTER RULES (enforced in prompts/system.php)
==============================================================================

Rule 1: Computed styles trump source code.
  Base44's Vite plugin injects styles at runtime; globals.css source values
  are often overridden. The scanner/scan-styles.js tool fetches the live URL
  and uses Puppeteer's getComputedStyle() to get actual values.

Rule 2: Never wp_enqueue_style for Google Fonts.
  esc_url() mangles CSS2 axis values. Use add_action('wp_head', ..., 5).

Rule 3: Tailwind line-height cascade.
  text-Xnl sets BOTH font-size AND line-height simultaneously.
  Responsive text-Xnl variants override standalone leading-* utilities.
  Always check for responsive variants (sm:/md:/lg:/xl:).

Rule 4: No blanket h1–h6 rules.
  Set font-family globally on h1–h6. All other properties (weight, size,
  line-height) must be set per component class, not globally.

Rule 5: Customizer required.
  Every theme must have WordPress Customizer support for:
  - Colors (primary, accent, background, text) — WP_Customize_Color_Control
  - Typography (heading_font, body_font, weights, sizes) — 25+ Google Fonts
  - transport: 'postMessage' for live preview where meaningful

Rule 6: Demo content importer.
  inc/demo-content.php must be included. Provides one-click demo setup
  accessible from Tools → {Theme Name} Demo Import.

Rule 7: Color extraction.
  Primary source: computed styles from live URL (Rule 1).
  Fallback: :root vars in globals.css.
  Fallback: Tailwind arbitrary [#hex] values in JSX/HTML.

Rule 8: Animation replacement.
  Framer Motion (Base44 uses it heavily) must be replaced with:
  CSS transitions/animations + IntersectionObserver for scroll triggers.
  No JS animation libraries in the output theme.

Rule 9: CSS architecture.
  BEM naming with theme prefix: .{prefix}-{block}__{element}--{modifier}
  CSS custom properties for all design tokens (:root vars).
  One theme.css file (no preprocessors).

Rule 10: HTML preflight.
  box-sizing: border-box on *, normalize margins, system font fallbacks,
  smooth scroll, font-smoothing. All in :root / * selector.

Rule 11: Naming conventions.
  CSS prefix = PHP prefix = text-domain = theme folder name = theme handle.
  Derived by slugifying the theme/app name (lowercase, hyphens, no specials).

