## SCANNER TOOL (scanner/scan-styles.js)
==============================================================================

WHY IT EXISTS: Rule 1 says computed live-site styles always override source
code. Base44's Vite build injects CSS at runtime, so globals.css often doesn't
reflect what the browser actually renders.

HOW TO USE:
  node scanner/scan-styles.js https://your-base44-app.com

WHAT IT DOES:
  1. Fetches HTML of the live URL
  2. Downloads all linked CSS files
  3. Parses :root {} custom properties from all CSS
  4. Scans class= attributes for Tailwind utility classes
  5. Detects Google Fonts <link> tags and extracts family names
  6. Extracts color values (hex, hsl, oklch, rgb)
  7. If puppeteer is installed: launches headless Chrome, calls
     getComputedStyle() on key elements for true computed values
  8. Outputs JSON: { colors, fonts, google_font_urls, css_vars }

The Converter passes this output to Analyzer.php to enrich the $data array.

